==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|l|u}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*loodak}}, from {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*loŋe-||to throw, push away}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|luo|da|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|uodɑ|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|/ˈluɔdɑ(ʔ)/}}

===Verb===
{{fi-verb}}
{{lb|fi|transitive}}

# to [[create]]
#: {{ux|fi|Alussa Jumala '''loi''' taivaan ja maan.|In the beginning God '''created''' the heaven and the earth. (Gen. 1:1)}}
# to [[shovel]] 
#: {{ux|fi|'''luoda''' lunta|to '''shovel''' snow|inline=1}}
# to [[shed]]
#: {{ux|fi|Lamppu '''luo''' sinistä valoa.|The lamp '''sheds''' blue light.}}
# {{lb|fi|always with an object}} to [[exuviate]], [[slough]], [[moult]], [[molt]] {{gloss|to shed or cast off a covering, especially a skin}}
#: {{ux|fi|Käärme alkoi '''luoda nahkaansa'''.|The snake began to '''moult'''.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Kun hummeri kasvaa, se '''luo kuorensa'''.|As it grows, a lobster will '''exuviate'''.}}
# {{lb|fi|archaic}} to begin, start <ref>Kolehmainen, T. 2001. ”Loihesi lausumahan”. Kieli-ikkuna. Helsingin Sanomat 14.8.2001. https://www.kotus.fi/nyt/kolumnit/kieli-ikkuna_(1996_2010)/loihesi_lausumahan</ref>

